fresh-eyes: independent cold reviewer (subagent, no authorship of this branch), full scope of the four commits moving Repo onto the mdstore capability.

Verdict LAND, given on 74a43b4. This tip is c9058ab, the same four
commits rebased onto another session's comment-only change to the gate
script. git diff between the two tips shows scripts/merge-gate.sh and
nothing else.

Two rounds. Round one returned DO-NOT-LAND on five items. The blocker
was a regression this branch introduced: opening the handle in
Repo::open made every command fail on a store whose note directory is
absent, which is any clone made before the first note. Four guards had
no test, and two of them together deleted a file outside the store.

Round two verified each fix by execution against a merge-base binary.
The absent-directory cases now match the merge base exactly. The
arbitrary delete is closed at resolve_id, which matched an exact id
with Path::exists and so followed a planted link; the reviewer
confirmed the hole did not move, checking every route downstream of
resolve_id and the slug generator.

Two mutations still survive the suite, and the reviewer verified that
each is honest redundancy rather than a gap: with resolve_id confined,
neither the id guard nor the confined delete is reachable alone.

39 tests, clippy clean, fmt clean, missouri 25 passed 0 failed, 70
steps, 1078 assertions.

Follow-ups recorded, none blocking: hold the handle lazily, which
closes a read-only corner and takes a mkdir off read commands; assert
the id guard's in-store half, an empty id and a dot name, which the
handle cannot refuse; drop a dead exists() probe in find_note.
